## P5a — remove the Lakebase graph-DB provisioner and superuser-grant flow

Context: Third increment of `.planning/databricks-decoupling/SPEC.md`. **Neo4j is now
kept** — the earlier plan to delete it is reversed, so `SecretsService.py` survives too
(it exists solely to back the Neo4j "Databricks secret" auth flow at
Settings → Back end → Neo4j). What P5 removes instead is the Lakebase-only control-plane
machinery: instance/branch/database creation and `DATABRICKS_SUPERUSER` grants. Neither
has any equivalent on a generic PostgreSQL server, and Azure Database for PostgreSQL
grants no true superuser at all — `azure_pg_admin` is deliberately not one, verified on
the provisioned server (`rolsuper = f`).

Removing this first also shrinks P2: `BranchLakebaseAuth` (projects/branches/endpoints)
